{"content":"h15.\n\nMemo visibility (\"who may view a memo\") is checked independently in each of these server surfaces — none of them share a single central gate, so each had to re-implement the PUBLIC/PROTECTED/PRIVATE rule:\n\n- Memo/comment read API (GetMemo, ListMemoComments) — `checkMemoReadAccess` in server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:39-68, called from memo_service.go:356,367 and memo_service_comments.go:148\n- Memo list/query API (ListMemos visibility filter) — server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:218-227 (and the analogous stats variant in server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go:84-90,218-220)\n- Comment creation API — server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:33-43 (checks the parent memo's visibility before allowing a comment)\n- Reaction API — server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:29-41 and :83 (ListReactions/UpsertReaction gate)\n- Attachment API (generic attachment service) — server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go:436-454\n- Memo-scoped attachment API — server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go:213-224\n- Raw file/attachment HTTP server — server/router/fileserver/fileserver.go:674-701 (separate from the gRPC attachment endpoints; also honors share tokens)\n- RSS feed generator — server/router/rss/rss.go:90 and :141 (hardcodes `VisibilityList: []store.Visibility{store.Public}`)\n- Frontend sitemap.xml — server/router/frontend/frontend.go:149-150 (same Public-only filter)\n- SSE real-time broadcast hub — server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go:134-144 (`canReceive` gates which connected clients get a memo event)\n- Email notification dispatch — server/notification/email.go:313-316\n- Mention-notification eligibility — server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:62-84\n\nThat's well over the \"at least three\" called for — the read-path (memo_service.go), the file-serving path (fileserver.go), and the syndication paths (rss.go / frontend.go sitemap) are the clearest distinct surfaces, with the API sub-resources (comments, reactions, attachments) and the async paths (SSE, email, mentions) each re-deriving the same PUBLIC/PROTECTED/PRIVATE logic on their own.","iteration":18,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
